  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/1"/>Let those who seek You, find You,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/2"/>those who rise early to entreat You,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/3"/>that the Accuser not prevail
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/4"/>and not seem wise in Your eyes;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/5"/>with [our] advocates and defenders—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/6"/>agree with them in Your kindness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/7"/>[say to them:] “Write concerning the Jews
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/8"/>as it is good in their eyes,”
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:bein_keseh_leasor/stanza_4/9"/>between Rosh Hashana and Yom Kippur.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
